/-!
# Native coefficient actions on actual regular-family derived stalks

Original complex and global holomorphic base functions act through the
native right-derived pushforward and native stalk functors. The genuine
neighborhood germs and global period-class germs respect those actions.
Actual all-degree fibre evaluation is complex-linear and sends a global
base multiplier to its original value at the base point.

The original degree-one evaluation has its explicit complex-linear
right inverse, while on open complex bases its raw-stalk kernel remains
nonzero. No local-ring module structure, local generation, local frame,
or residue-field base-change isomorphism is asserted here.
-/
